#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "There are two support collection methods, the first utilizes the legacy flow-tools binaries and the second leverages Cacti's own PHP based flow stream server."
msgstr "Postoje dvije podržane metode prikupljanja: prva koristi naslijeđene izvršne datoteke flow-tools, a druga koristi vlastiti Cacti PHP server za tok podataka."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Bind to address"
msgstr "Veži za adresu"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "If Cacti server has more IP Addresses, you can specify specific interface. Leave as 0.0.0.0 for primary interface."
msgstr "Ako Cacti server ima više IP adresa, možete navesti određeni interfejs. Ostavite 0.0.0.0 za primarni interfejs."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Allowed Host Range"
msgstr "Dozvoljeni opseg hostova"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "IP Address of the device that is allowed to send to this flow collector.  Leave as 0.0.0.0 for any host.  Note that PHP is finicky about what it allows.  CIDR syntax is supported as well as range syntax for example 192.168.1.0 or 192.168.1.0/24.  If you want specific IP addresses, separate them by a comma."
msgstr "IP adresa uređaja kojem je dozvoljeno slanje ovom sakupljaču tokova. Ostavite 0.0.0.0 za bilo koji host. Imajte na umu da je PHP izbirljiv u pogledu onoga što dozvoljava. Podržana je CIDR sintaksa, kao i sintaksa opsega, na primjer 192.168.1.0 ili 192.168.1.0/24. Ako želite određene IP adrese, odvojite ih zarezom."

